<title>NEW ZEALAND: Mercury-Utilicorp NZ challenge goes to High Court.</title>
<headline>Mercury-Utilicorp NZ challenge goes to High Court.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mercury Energy Ltd's challenge of UtiliCorp NZ Ltd's agreements with four local councils regarding their Power New Zealand Ltd shares went to the High Court in Auckland on Monday.</p>
<p>The hearing, which is being held in chambers, is expected to last two days.</p>
<p>The councils, in the former Valley Power region, collectively own 7.1 percent of Power NZ.  </p>
<p>The verbal agreements which Mercury is challenging gave the councils a right to put their Power NZ shares with UtiliCorp and gave UtiliCorp a right of first refusal should they wish to sell.</p>
<p>UtiliCorp NZ, about 80-percent owned by UtiliCorp United Inc, has been locked in a takeover battle with Mercury over Power NZ for almost two years.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
</text>
